1
00:04:40,909 --> 00:04:46,909
Vengeance is the ultimate weapon.

2
00:09:21,818 --> 00:09:27,818
War is a action, crime, thriller film directed by Philip G. Atwell.

3
00:14:02,727 --> 00:14:08,727
FBI agent Jack Crawford is out for revenge when his partner is killed
and all clues point to the mysterious assassin Rogue.

4
00:18:43,636 --> 00:18:49,636
But when Rogue turns up years later to take care of some unfinished
business, he triggers a violent clash of rival gangs.

5
00:23:24,545 --> 00:23:30,545
Will the truth come out before it's too late?

6
00:28:05,454 --> 00:28:11,454
And when the dust settles, who will remain standing?

7
00:32:46,363 --> 00:32:52,363
Rogue, played by Jet Li.

8
00:37:27,272 --> 00:37:33,272
Special Agent Jack Crawford, played by Jason Statham.

9
00:42:08,181 --> 00:42:14,181
Li Chang, played by John Lone.

10
00:46:49,090 --> 00:46:55,090
Shiro Yanagawa, played by Ryo Ishibashi.

11
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:36,000
Kira Yanagawa, played by Devon Aoki.

12
00:56:10,909 --> 00:56:16,909
Wu Ti, played by Mark Cheng Ho-Nam.

13
01:00:51,818 --> 01:00:57,818
War is a 2007 American action film directed by Philip G.

14
01:05:32,727 --> 01:05:38,727
Atwell in his directorial debut and featuring stage
combat choreographed by Corey Yuen.

15
01:10:13,636 --> 01:10:19,636
The film stars Jet Li and Jason Statham.

16
01:14:54,545 --> 01:15:00,545
Jason Statham plays an FBI agent determined to take down a mysterious assassin
known as Rogue (played by Jet Li), after his partner is murdered.

17
01:19:35,454 --> 01:19:41,454
War features the second collaboration between Jet Li and Jason Statham,
reuniting them for the first time since 2001 film The One.

18
01:24:16,363 --> 01:24:22,363
War's working title was Rogue; it was changed to avoid
conflict with another film with the same name.

19
01:28:57,272 --> 01:29:03,272
It was re-titled as Rogue Assassin in New Zealand, Japan, Hong Kong, Singapore,
India, Australia, the Philippines and several European countries.

20
01:33:38,181 --> 01:33:44,181
The film was released in the United States on August 24, 2007, receiving negative reviews from
critics and grossed $40.7 million at the box office against the $25 million budget.

21
01:38:19,090 --> 01:38:25,090
The tone is dark and intense.
